.TH portensor 1  "portensor 1.0.0-rc.1"
.SH NAME
portensor \- An accuracy\-first TCP port scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBportensor\fR [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-db\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-scripts\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
An accuracy\-first TCP/UDP scanner. Portensor uses a bounded worker pool, adaptive per\-host timeouts, a global rate limit, and a short service\-verification read so a bare handshake from a tarpit or SYN proxy is not reported as an open service. Responsive services are identified from their banners, including common products and versions. With raw\-socket support (Linux root/CAP_NET_RAW, or Windows with Npcap), \-\-syn performs raw SYN discovery and verifies responsive candidates over TCP. A UDP scanner is available for service detection on ports that accept UDP traffic.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR
Color theme for tables, progress, and diagnostics
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
hacker
.IP \(bu 2
minimal
.IP \(bu 2
cyber
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Structured diagnostic level for stderr (also PORTENSOR_LOG)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
error
.IP \(bu 2
warn
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
debug
.IP \(bu 2
trace
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory for the local NVD advisory database
.TP
\fB\-\-scripts\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory for the local script pack library
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
portensor\-scan(1)
Scan TCP ports on one or more targets
.TP
portensor\-diff(1)
Compare two previous scan reports or state files to display differences
.TP
portensor\-merge(1)
Merge reports from distributed/sharded scans into one report
.TP
portensor\-distributed(1)
Plan, coordinate, or execute distributed scans across multiple hosts
.TP
portensor\-doctor(1)
Check permissions, terminal support, and scan capabilities
.TP
portensor\-db(1)
Manage the local NVD CVE advisory database
.TP
portensor\-probes(1)
List built\-in and custom probe packs
.TP
portensor\-scripts(1)
List and validate script plugin manifests (sidecar or WASM)
.TP
portensor\-interactive(1)
Set up and run a scan with guided prompts
.TP
portensor\-smart(1)
Build an explainable scan plan, then execute it unless \-\-dry\-run is set
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  portensor scan \-\-target 127.0.0.1 \-\-ports 1\-1024
  portensor scan \-t 10.0.0.0/24 \-p 22,80,443 \-\-json
  portensor scan \-t 10.77.0.2 \-p 1\-10000 \-\-profile careful \-\-show all
  portensor scan \-t 10.77.0.2 \-\-scripts ./scripts \-\-json
  portensor scripts list ./scripts \-\-json
  portensor scripts install ./my\-pack
  portensor scan \-t 10.77.0.2 \-\-scripts\-library
  portensor db intel \-\-force
  sudo portensor scan \-6 \-t fe80::/64 \-\-ndp \-p 22,80,443
.SH VERSION
v1.0.0\-rc.1
